## 4. Role Transition Rules

| From | To | Condition | Process |
|---|---|---|---|
| Anonymous Donor | Registered Donor | User creates account | Self-service registration |
| Registered Donor | Campaign Creator | User creates first campaign | Automatic role upgrade on campaign creation |
| Campaign Creator | Campaign Creator | Always — cannot be downgraded | Permanent after first campaign |
| Any User | Admin | Manual assignment | Platform owner assigns via Supabase Dashboard |

---

## 5. Session & Authentication

| Aspect | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Auth Provider | Supabase Auth (email/password) |
| Session Storage | iOS Keychain (via Supabase Swift SDK) |
| Session Duration | Until explicit logout |
| Token Refresh | Automatic by Supabase SDK |
| Role Check | Query `users` table for `role` column |
| Admin Check | `users.role = 'admin'` AND valid Supabase session |

---

## 6. Security Principles

1. **Principle of Least Privilege**: Each role has the minimum permissions needed.
2. **Defense in Depth**: RLS + application-level checks + Edge Function validation.
3. **Data Isolation**: Users cannot access other users' data.
4. **Admin Privilege Escalation Protection**: Admin role assigned only via backend.
5. **Immutable Financial Records**: No user role can modify completed donation records.
6. **Audit Trail**: All verification decisions logged with admin ID and timestamp.
